        "abstract": "Directional Currents Method, which was developed and tested for rectangular horn antennas recently by Polat and Daşbaşı, is applied to derive explicit radiation fields of a conical horn antenna located over a simple lossy dielectric half-space. The influence of presence of transmission medium on E- and H-plane radiation performances of the conical horn is displayed under dominant mode excitation in comparison with similar results for a pyramidal horn in X-band. The accuracy of the radiation fields when the conical horn is located close to air-ocean interface is checked by comparing with the full wave simulation data of the commercial software CST<sup xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">TM</sup>.",
